    "id": "art-2026-11-21-cleveland-browns-upset-steelers-snow-thursday-football",
    "slug": "nick-chubb-powers-browns-snowstorm-upset-over-steelers-thursday-night-football",
    "title": "Nick Chubb's Two Touchdowns Power Cleveland Browns to 24-19 Snowstorm Upset Over Pittsburgh Steelers on Thursday Night Football",
    "excerpt": "In a throwback AFC North classic played in heavy lake-effect snowfall, Nick Chubb scored two rushing touchdowns, including the game-winner with 57 seconds left, to lead the underdog Cleveland Browns past Russell Wilson and the 8-3 Pittsburgh Steelers.",
    "content": [
      "CLEVELAND — In a breathtaking, whiteout slugfest that instantly entered the lore of legendary AFC North rivalries, the underdog Cleveland Browns weathered blinding lake-effect snow squalls and a fierce fourth-quarter comeback to shock the division-leading Pittsburgh Steelers 24-19 on Thursday Night Football at Huntington Bank Field. Running back Nick Chubb authored an unforgettable chapter in his celebrated career, bulling his way into the end zone for two rushing touchdowns—including the game-winning 2-yard plunge with just 57 seconds remaining on the game clock.",
      "Played in treacherous, freezing conditions off the shores of Lake Erie, the contest was defined by swirling 30-mile-per-hour wind gusts and heavy blanket snowfall that forced stadium grounds crews to deploy snowplows and shovels during timeouts to uncover yard lines and end zone boundaries. Under the snowy canopy, Browns quarterback Jameis Winston demonstrated poise and tactical grit, completing 18 of 27 passes for 219 yards, while scoring on a rugged 8-yard quarterback keeper to open the scoring in the first half.",
      "However, the emotional heart of the night belonged to Chubb, facing the very franchise against which he suffered a catastrophic, season-ending knee injury fourteen months prior. Battling through knee-deep slush and a suffocating Pittsburgh defensive front, Chubb carried 20 times for 59 grueling yards, repeatedly moving the chains on critical third-down conversions. His final touchdown drive saw Winston engineer a flawless 11-play, 61-yard march through the snow, capping it off by handing the ball to Chubb, who drove through two defenders to break the plane and send the frostbitten home crowd into pandemonium.",
      "Defensively, reigning NFL Defensive Player of the Year Myles Garrett put on an absolute masterclass in edge rushing dominance against Pittsburgh's offensive line. Garrett sacked Steelers quarterback Russell Wilson three times in the second half alone, forcing a critical fumble and generating seven quarterback pressures that prevented Pittsburgh from establishing their customary vertical passing rhythm. Wilson finished 21 of 28 for 270 yards and a touchdown pass to Calvin Austin III, but was repeatedly harassed on the Steelers' frantic final drive.",
      "The dramatic finish culminated on the game's final play from the Cleveland 39-yard line. With four seconds remaining, Wilson took the shotgun snap and lofted a desperation Hail Mary pass into a swirling blizzard toward the end zone. Browns safety Grant Delpit and cornerback Denzel Ward leaped among a cluster of Steelers receivers, batting the ball harmlessly onto the snow-covered turf as the final buzzer sounded, setting off wild celebrations on the Cleveland sideline.",
      "The victory, while improving the Browns' record to 3-8, severely disrupted the AFC North championship race, dropping the Steelers to 8-3 and narrowing their lead over the surging Baltimore Ravens. For Browns head coach Kevin Stefanski and a locker room that has navigated devastating injuries and offensive turbulence all season, the snowy triumph proved that in the bitter chill of late-November football, sheer heart, physical toughness, and defensive grit can triumph over any odds."
    ],
