      "SEATTLE — A historic and ferocious extratropical storm system characterized by meteorologists as a 'once-in-a-decade bomb cyclone' slammed into the Pacific Northwest and Northern California on Wednesday, unleashing destructive hurricane-force wind gusts exceeding 80 miles per hour, torrential coastal deluges, and paralyzing blizzard conditions across mountainous passes. The extraordinary storm—which underwent explosive cyclogenesis by dropping an astounding 70 millibars of central atmospheric pressure in less than 24 hours—claimed at least two lives in western Washington and plunged more than 600,000 homes and commercial businesses into total darkness.",
      "Emergency management directors and first responders across Puget Sound faced catastrophic conditions throughout Wednesday night as saturated soils gave way beneath howling winds, sending towering Douglas fir and cedar trees crashing onto residential roofs, arterial highways, and primary electrical distribution grids. In Lynnwood and Bellevue, Washington, emergency crews responded to fatal tree collapses that crushed occupied homes. Puget Sound Energy and Seattle City Light declared systemic emergencies, mobilizing thousands of specialized lineworkers from across the western United States to repair hundreds of downed transmission towers and severed sub-stations.",
