      "GENEVA / ATLANTA — In a stark and urgent warning regarding the fragile state of global pediatric public health, the World Health Organization (WHO) and the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) released a joint epidemiological surveillance report on Wednesday documenting an alarming 20% surge in global measles infections. According to verified health surveillance models, an estimated 10.3 million individuals worldwide contracted the highly contagious viral pathogen in the past year, resulting in approximately 107,500 deaths—the overwhelming majority of which claimed the lives of young children under the age of five in vulnerable, low-income nations.",
