      "However, the failure to meet clean audit standards triggered sharp bipartisan condemnation across both chambers of Congress, where lawmakers are finalizing language for the upcoming National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA). Prominent members of the Senate Armed Services and Budget Committees reiterated their commitment to enacting legislative enforcement mechanisms that would penalize military branches failing to secure unmodified audit opinions. Proposed provisions include mandatory 0.5% budgetary withholdings, recurring sequester rescissions on departmental civilian administrative accounts, and heightened executive reporting mandates for non-compliant procurement programs.",
