      "The policy summit comes as local municipal leaders, mayors, and non-profit humanitarian organizations along the Rio Grande Valley voice urgent concerns regarding humanitarian resources, medical capacities, and legal representation access. Representatives from international refugee advocacy coalitions cautioned that tightening preliminary screening thresholds without expanding legal immigration pathways or providing adequate consular personnel risks stranding thousands of vulnerable migrants in perilous, cartel-dominated encampments across northern Mexican border states.",
      "Simultaneously, commercial freight operators, international trade associations, and logistics executives in attendance emphasized the critical imperative of safeguarding lawful cross-border commerce. Border crossings such as Laredo's World Trade Bridge and El Paso's Ysleta Port of Entry process more than $800 billion in annual bilateral manufactured goods, automotive components, and agricultural freight. Trade leaders urged federal authorities to ensure that stepped-up cargo and passenger inspections do not result in crippling logistical bottlenecks or supply-chain disruptions for North American manufacturing sectors.",
